{"event": "model_response", "time": 1793848052.2718825, "run_id": "10639db121d146fa9696d9099c6f2d6e", "seq": 8, "number": 1, "response": {"id": "50d19898-560f-4025-a614-6c3ef2bb4201", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1793848049, "model": "deepseek-flash", "choices": [{"index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Inspect the current plan and baseline state before reading or editing.\n\n```python\nprint(task_status())\n```", "reasoning_content": "We need act as agent to read paper. We have tools. Need plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json, read_pdf full range. Must follow workflow. Need write notes for five topics and submit report. Important max 40 requests, currently request 1, plenty. Need be efficient.\n\nFirst update_plan then baseline pytest, read files. We can do multiple actions per turn? Contract says briefly describe next action, output ONE fenced Python block and STOP. We can execute several statements in one block. We need plan first before editing. Baseline checks. Let's do update_plan and run pytest? \"Use update_plan before editing and run baseline checks.\" We can do plan and baseline in one block. Read report.json/paper.json maybe also same? Need baseline first. We can print task status? Let's do update_plan with plan items. Titles/order must retain existing titles/order if any. We don't know existing plan. task_status gives plan. First call task_status."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 4594, "completion_tokens": 230, "total_tokens": 4824, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 128}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 208}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4466}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
