64385e22f3c5\"],\n    section=\"overview\",\n)\nprint(r)\n```", "reasoning_content": "I need to continue reading pending batches. Pending evidence ids correspond to pages 7-52 presumably. Let me call recall on pending ids? Actually the instruction: \"Continue the pending batch; do not reread unchanged sources. Write notes only from originals already received.\" The delivery advances automatically after successful actions. So I should take an action (e.g., write_note) to trigger next batch delivery. But I should first update the overview note with the literature selection facts (Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM, snowballing approach) — that answers search_methods.\n\nLet me write the overview note now with categories and search methods, plus quotes with page numbers.\n\nNote content must be 20..1500 chars. Include: categories: reason, act, interact (verb base forms). search_methods: google_scholar_search, snowballing (lowercase, underscores).\n\nQuotes: page 5: \"The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.\"\n\nAlso categories quote from page 4/1: \"Agents that receive input in natural language from their environment, reason to make decisions, and take autonomous actions...\" Abstract quote maybe page 1. I have ev for page 4 and 5. Categories quote from page 4: \"agents may receive input and reason in natural or formal language\" hmm. Better: need a quote supporting reason, act, interact. Page 4 has \"The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other\". That supports all three. Good.\n\nLet me write the note and then next batch triggers."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8794, "completion_tokens": 760, "total_tokens": 9554, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 352}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 435