iew', 'content': \"overview (p4-5): categories = reason, act, interact; p4 defines agentic LLMs as agents that receive input in natural language, reason to make decisions, and take autonomous actions, and states 'The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other'. Literature Selection p5: initially a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM, then a snowballing approach for cited work not in the initial set; only LLM-based approaches kept. search_methods = google_scholar_search, snowballing. Quote p5: 'The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.'\", 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2', 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5'], 'valid': True, 'request': 5}}, 'answers': {}, 'section_text': {}}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 7330, "output_tokens": 342, "total_tokens": 7672}, "is_final_answer": false}}
