ne in p['text'].split('\\n'): if any(k in line for k in kws): print(p['page'], line[:300])\n\nKeywords: Toolformer, ToolBench, API, CAMEL, Generative Agents, evaluator, Table 4, agenda.\n\nDo read_pdf ranges: (24,30), (36,42), (47,52)? That's 20 pages of text; the tool returns them as batches... may be huge. Restrict to smaller: tool use maybe 26-28. Hmm, unknown.\n\nActually, section order: 2.x reasoning (p9-18), 3? Let me think: paper structure: 1 Introduction, 2 Reasoning (p9-18), 3 Acting/tool use (p19-28?), 4 Interacting (p30-40), 5? Then 7 Discussion/agenda p44-50.\n\nI'll read (24,29), (33,40), (44,52) → 22 pages. That's a lot but printing only keywords.\n\nLet's do it."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8722, "completion_tokens": 1599, "total_tokens": 10321, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1419}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4370}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
